    15 views in public schema were owned by postgres and lacked
    security_invoker=on, bypassing RLS on base tables when called with
    anon key. Anon could read 12 leads (PII), owner earnings, damages,
    protection cases, growth metrics, etc.
    
    Fix: ALTER VIEW SET (security_invoker = on) on all 15 (applied to
    production as migration fase_82_security_invoker_views). Verified
    via REST with anon key: all 8 sensitive views return 0 rows.
    Admin/owner/client legitimate access unaffected.
    
